.TH SESSION-WORKBENCH 1 "@DATE@" "session-workbench @VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
session-workbench \- run many Claude Code sessions side by side
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B session-workbench
.RB [ \-config
.IR file ]
.br
.B session-workbench
.B \-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B session-workbench
is a desktop application for working with many Claude Code sessions at once.
Each session is bound to one directory and has five tabs, by default in this
order:
.TP
.B Local
a shell on this computer in the same directory;
.TP
.B Files
the directory as a tree, with git status markers and a check for
repository hooks and settings that git on this computer would run;
.TP
.B Remote
a terminal connected with
.BR ssh (1)
to an agent host, inside a
.BR tmux (1)
session that runs
.B claude
(or a shell) in that directory; it survives closing the application and lost
connections;
.TP
.B Notes
notes about the project, stored next to the configuration file, not in the
project. A separate notes page for all sessions holds prompts you use often
and can paste them into the current session's Remote tab;
.TP
.B Web
the repository's latest GitHub Actions runs (with
.BR gh (1))
and links to its web pages.
.PP
The agent host gets at the directory through a shared file system, a live
share over ssh (the agent host mounts it with
.BR sshfs (1)),
or a working copy sent with
.BR rsync (1)
(or a built-in tar transfer where rsync is missing) whose commits are fetched back with
.BR git (1).
Agent and X11 forwarding are always disabled on these ssh connections.
.PP
Claude Code's data on each agent host
.RI ( ~/.claude
and
.IR ~/.claude.json ,
without claude's login) is copied to this computer, every hour by default,
while the application runs, so a lost agent host can be restored.
.PP
When claude waits for input in a session you are not looking at, the session
is marked and a desktop notification is shown.
.PP
Only one instance runs per configuration file; starting it again brings the
running window to the front.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-config " file"
Use
.I file
instead of the default configuration file. The lock file and the
.I notes
directory are kept next to it.
.TP
.B \-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/session-workbench/config.toml
Hosts, sessions, folders and settings (honours
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ).
The application reads it at start and rewrites it on every change; hand edits
are fine while it is not running. Unknown keys are rejected, and a file that
cannot be read is never overwritten.
.TP
.I ~/.config/session-workbench/config.toml.lock
Keeps a second instance from using the same configuration.
.TP
.I ~/.config/session-workbench/notes/
The Notes tab's files, one per session, and
.I _app.md
for the notes page of all sessions.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/session-workbench/
Claude backups of the agent hosts
.RI ( claude-backups/ <host>/ )
and window state (honours
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR tmux (1),
.BR sshfs (1),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR git (1),
.BR gh (1)
.PP
https://github.com/maarten-boot/multi-session-ssh-dev, in particular
docs/CONNECTIVITY.md for setting up agent hosts and the security model.
